
## plan review: one findings round, then clean
$ next-step.sh rp plan status=ready file=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/plan.md summary=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/plan.summary.md
next=review
do: spawn the plan reviewer
see: ### Gate 2 — plan and tracking issue
$ next-step.sh rp plan status=findings file=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/review.md summary=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/review.verdict.md count=2 user=0
logged: plan-review=findings count=2 round=1
next=revise
run: cp .claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/plan.md .claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/plan.prev.md
do: resume the planner with the review file
see: ### Gate 2 — plan and tracking issue
$ next-step.sh rp plan status=ready file=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/plan.md summary=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/plan.summary.md
next=follow-up
do: spawn the plan reviewer again for a follow-up round
see: ### Gate 2 — plan and tracking issue
$ next-step.sh rp plan status=clean file=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/review.md summary=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/review.verdict.md
logged: plan-review=clean round=2
next=issue
do: ask the spec author for the tracking issue
see: ### Gate 2 — plan and tracking issue

## fast lane after an architecture stop: gate 2 is a notice
$ next-step.sh rp plan status=new file=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/issue.md
next=notice
run: sh .claude/scripts/prompt-render.sh gate2-notice rp issue=new
do: show the notice without stopping, then act on approval as if given
see: ### Gate 2 — plan and tracking issue
$ prompt-render.sh gate2-notice rp issue=new
Gate 2 · rp · 2 code stages. · issue new · starting s0 (pre-authorized — say stop to hold)
Confirm: nothing flagged
$ card-move.sh rp inprogress
$ card-move.sh rp.s0 inprogress
$ card-log.sh rp.s0 green
$ card-move.sh rp.s0 inreview
impl: status=inreview stage=s0 delta=0
$ card-log.sh rp.s0 commit=1b8d0dd
impl: status=committed stage=s0 sha=1b8d0dd delta=0
$ sha-check.sh rp s0 1b8d0dd
sha=ok
$ card-log.sh rp gauntlet=pass cov=81% sha=1b8d0dd
$ card-move.sh rp.s0 done

## s1 test first: red for the right reason, then green with a spec change
$ card-move.sh rp.s1 inprogress
$ card-log.sh rp.s1 test-red MB-R-001 -- it_read_last: expected 65535, got an error
$ card-log.sh rp.s1 green
$ card-log.sh rp.s1 spec-delta MB-R-002 added origin=impl -- the wrap at 65535 was unstated
$ card-move.sh rp.s1 inreview
$ card-log.sh rp.s1 commit=0feb5e7
impl: status=committed stage=s1 sha=0feb5e7 delta=1
$ sha-check.sh rp s1 0feb5e7
sha=ok
$ card-log.sh rp gauntlet=pass cov=81% sha=0feb5e7

## the delta review needs the user: delta stop, the user overturns the recommendation
$ prompt-render.sh delta rp stage=s1
Question · rp · delta s1 · spec-reviewer · 1 decision
## 1. 1. MB-R-002 added: keep the wrap rule?
Options:
- a) keep (recommended)
- b) revert
Answer: <1: a · 2: b · …> · other <text> — keep, revert or split each change
user: 1: b
$ card-log.sh rp overturned scope=delta count=1 -- user reverted the wrap rule
$ card-move.sh rp.s1 done

## s2 green
$ card-move.sh rp.s2 inprogress
$ card-log.sh rp.s2 green
$ card-move.sh rp.s2 inreview
impl: status=inreview stage=s2 delta=0
$ card-log.sh rp.s2 commit=dd0c1fb
impl: status=committed stage=s2 sha=dd0c1fb delta=0
$ sha-check.sh rp s2 dd0c1fb
sha=ok
$ card-log.sh rp gauntlet=pass cov=81% sha=dd0c1fb
$ card-move.sh rp.s2 done
board:
  inprogress/rp.md
  done/rp.s0.md
  done/rp.s1.md
  done/rp.s2.md

## branch review: one finding fixed, then clean
$ card-move.sh rp inreview
$ next-step.sh rp branch status=findings file=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/review.md summary=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/review.verdict.md count=1 user=0
logged: review=1-open scope=branch
next=fix
do: move the implicated stage to inprogress, resume its implementer, gauntlet, then a fresh branch review
see: ### Gate 3 — review
$ card-move.sh rp.s2 inprogress
$ card-log.sh rp.s2 green
$ card-move.sh rp.s2 inreview
$ card-log.sh rp.s2 commit=af11706
impl: status=committed stage=s2 sha=af11706 delta=0
$ sha-check.sh rp s2 af11706
sha=ok
$ card-log.sh rp gauntlet=pass cov=81% sha=af11706
$ card-move.sh rp.s2 done
$ next-step.sh rp branch status=clean file=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/review.md summary=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/review.verdict.md
logged: review=1-resolved
next=pr
do: spawn the spec author for the PR body
see: ### Gate 4 — pull request

## gate 4 shows the verdict
$ next-step.sh rp pr status=ready file=.claude/tasks/artifacts/rp/pr.md follow-ups=0
next=stop
run: sh .claude/scripts/prompt-render.sh gate4 rp
do: show the gate 4 stop and wait for the user's approval
see: ### Gate 4 — pull request
$ prompt-render.sh gate4 rp pr=9
Gate 4 · rp · pr.md, review.verdict.md · fast lane
PR: Read register 65535
Review: clean — ready for approval
Not checked: nothing
Spec: 2 of 2 pinned
Approving will:
- push, replace the draft's title and body, mark #9 ready
- wait for CI, clean up
Answer: approve · change <what> · re-plan: <why> · stop (hold, e.g. for a manual run first)
user: approve
$ prompt-render.sh approved rp
approved

## CI red: clean-up refuses until the fix lands
$ next-step.sh rp ci ci=1
logged: ci=1
next=fix
run: bash .claude/scripts/failed-workflow.sh feat/rp
do: read the failed workflow and fix it
see: ### Gate 4 — pull request
$ run-cleanup.sh rp
cleanup=refused reason=ci-red
$ card-move.sh rp.s1 inprogress
$ card-log.sh rp.s1 green

## the fix's commit is refused until its card moves
$ card-log.sh rp.s1 commit=0badc0d
card-log=reject event=commit reason=inprogress move=inreview
$ card-move.sh rp.s1 inreview
$ card-log.sh rp.s1 commit=d6043f4
impl: status=committed stage=s1 sha=d6043f4 delta=0
$ sha-check.sh rp s1 d6043f4
sha=ok
$ card-log.sh rp gauntlet=pass cov=81% sha=d6043f4
$ card-move.sh rp.s1 done

## CI green: clean-up records the metrics and archives the run
$ next-step.sh rp ci ci=0
logged: ci=0
next=done
run: sh .claude/scripts/run-cleanup.sh rp
do: clean up the run
see: ### Clean up
$ run-cleanup.sh rp
cleanup=done archive=<R>/.claude/tasks/archive/rp
metrics.log:
rp start=2026-10-05T09:00 end=2026-10-05T18:00 first-red=2026-10-05T09:00 stages=3 stops=2 question=0 approval=2 stage=0 blocked=0 replans=0 overturned=1 reads=0 lane=fast ci=0
board:
exit=0
